      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. \"Exploratory design\" sounds much better than \"limited sample.\" \n\nBut looking at the current draft, we haven't actually labeled it as exploratory yet—we've presented it as a primary study. If we change the labeling now to match that \"depth of data\" angle, do you think we can skip the explicit limitations paragraph altogether? I'd rather we present this as a highly controlled, high-fidelity study where the small N is actually an asset for precision, rather than admitting it's a constraint.",
